{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job deselects tests known to fail on Windows through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-api.args`. This bug owns that file: 27 `--deselect` lines plus `--ignore=tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py`, from the scheduled runs at `b4e0d01b649` (2026-11-15/16). Each failure uses a POSIX-only API on Windows with no Windows path. Evidence per group, read from the Windows job logs of runs 43820680079, 43871224211 and the `b4e0d01b649` run:\n\n1. Product: `rebar.llm.gate_admission` imports `fcntl` directly (`src/rebar/llm/gate_admission.py:25-28`, `flock` at :244 and :270) and disarms the concurrency cap on Windows (`:333-336`, reason \"advisory locking (fcntl) unavailable\"). The store already has a portable exclusive-lock leg with a Windows `msvcrt.locking` branch: `rebar._store.lock_kernel.take_exclusive` / `release_exclusive` / `leg_name` (`src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py:111-156`). Failing: `test_gate_admission_09da.py::test_a_platform_without_proc_meminfo_admits_silently` and `::test_an_unusable_slot_file_admits_and_announces_the_disarm` (both see the fcntl disarm marker).\n2. Product: `rebar.grounding.harness.run_in_worker` maps a worker crash to `parse_error` only for a negative exit code (`src/rebar/grounding/harness.py:385-395`). A native crash on Windows exits with an NTSTATUS code (for example `0xC0000005`, access violation), which is positive, so it lands in `other`. The test payload `tests/unit/grounding/_worker_payloads.py:52-65` sends itself `signal.SIGKILL`, which does not exist on Windows (`AttributeError`, so the worker \"raised\"). Failing: `grounding/test_harness.py::test_worker_hard_crash_maps_to_parse_error_not_host_crash`, `grounding/test_conformance.py::test_worker_crash_does_not_take_down_host`.\n3. Collection: `tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py:201` uses `-signal.SIGKILL` in a module-level `parametrize`, so the module fails to collect on Windows. That collection error is the whole cause of `test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_make_test_never_selects_a_live_test_even_with_jira_credentials_set` and `test_collection_isolation_guard.py::test_the_live_unit_tier_collects_clean` (their logs show only `ERROR tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py - AttributeError: module 'signal' has no attribute 'SIGKILL'`).\n4. Test stub: `tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py:83-87` replaces `_proc.subprocess` with a `SimpleNamespace` holding only `Popen` and `DEVNULL`; on Windows `_proc._detach_kwargs` (`src/rebar/_proc.py:112-121`) reads `subprocess.DETACHED_PROCESS` from it (4 tests). `:123-124` also asserts the POSIX kwargs unconditionally.\n5. Tests that exercise a POSIX-only leg by design, with no capability guard: `fcntl` leg tests patching `_kernel.fcntl.flock` while `fcntl` is `None` (`test_lock_stale_reclaim.py` 6, `test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084.py` 2); the `fcntl` availability control (`test_fcntl_import_guard.py::test_fcntl_available_here_control`); `resource`-based peak-RSS reads (`test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3.py` 2; `peak_rss_bytes` already returns `None` without `resource`, `src/rebar/llm/peak_rss.py:40-48`); signal-killed children (`test_live_dc_pass_health.py` 2, `test_external_mutation_diagnostics.py` 1); in-process SIGTERM handler grace (`tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py::test_sigterm_grace_subprocess_waits_for_inflight_then_exits_zero`: on Windows `os.kill(pid, SIGTERM)` is `TerminateProcess`, exit 15, so no handler runs); `os.getuid`/`os.geteuid` (`tests/scripts/test_gerrit_object_store_repair.py:72,92`, which drives the Linux host script `infra/scripts/materialize-gerrit-jgit-config.sh` that `chown`s to a uid:gid; `tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py:517`).\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the product where Windows has a real equivalent, and guard tests on the missing capability where the behaviour is POSIX-only by design. This keeps every product guarantee intact and matches the precedent `src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py` set for the store lock.\n\n- `gate_admission`: drop the direct `fcntl` import and take slots through `lock_kernel.take_exclusive` (non-blocking on both legs) and `release_exclusive`. Disarm only when `lock_kernel.leg_name() == \"none\"`, with reason \"no exclusive file-lock primitive (fcntl or msvcrt) available\". On Windows the cap is then in force instead of disarmed.\n- `grounding.harness`: extract the exit-status classification into a small pure function and also treat a Windows exit code with the NTSTATUS error severity (`>= 0xC0000000`) as a crash (`parse_error`), naming the code in hex in `detail`. `hard_crash` keeps SIGKILL on POSIX and on Windows exits with the access-violation status (`os._exit(-1073741819)`, reported by the OS as `0xC0000005`), which is the exit status the harness observes for a real native crash.\n- `test_bridge_runner_spawn.py:201`: use the literal returncode `-9` (the value under test), so the module collects everywhere.\n- `test_spawn_detached.py`: build the stub from the real module (`SimpleNamespace(**vars(subprocess))` with `Popen` overridden), and assert the platform's own detach kwargs.\n- Capability guards: `pytest.mark.skipif(_kernel.fcntl is None, ...)` on the fcntl-leg tests; `pytest.importorskip(\"fcntl\")` / `(\"resource\")` in the control and peak-RSS tests; `skipif(not hasattr(signal, \"SIGKILL\"))` on the signal-death tests; `skipif(os.name == \"nt\")` with the TerminateProcess reason on the SIGTERM-grace test; `skipif(not hasattr(os, \"getuid\"))` on the Linux host-script test; and `not hasattr(os, \"geteuid\") or os.geteuid() == 0` selects the already-present simulated-failure branch in `test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py`.\n- Remove every line from `posix-api.args`, delete the file, and drop its `@` reference from `.github/workflows/test.yml` (`tests/unit/test_windows_sweep_deselect.py` keeps the two in step).\n\nPortability: no new POSIX-only API is introduced. The new code paths use `msvcrt` through the existing `lock_kernel` leg and `os._exit`, both present on Windows.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/gate_admission.py`, `src/rebar/grounding/harness.py`\n- `tests/unit/grounding/_worker_payloads.py`, `tests/unit/grounding/test_harness.py`, `tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py` (the no-leg disarm test patches `lock_kernel.fcntl`/`msvcrt` to `None`; the non-blocking spy test spies `lock_kernel.take_exclusive`)\n- `tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py`, `tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py`, `tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py`, `tests/unit/test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084.py`, `tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py`, `tests/unit/test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3.py`, `tests/unit/test_live_dc_pass_health.py`, `tests/unit/test_external_mutation_diagnostics.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py`, `tests/scripts/test_gerrit_object_store_repair.py`\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-api.args` (deleted), `.github/workflows/test.yml`\n\n## Testing\n\n- New unit tests for the harness classifier (run on every platform): a negative exit code maps to `parse_error` naming the signal; `0xC0000005` maps to `parse_error` naming the hex status on Windows; a plain positive exit (`3`) and a Windows exit below `0xC0000000` stay `other`.\n- Gate admission on POSIX: the existing congestion, release and disarm tests still pass through `lock_kernel`; failure path: with both legs patched to `None` the admission disarms with the new reason.\n- `make verify` passes. After merge, a dispatched `sweep (windows)` run on main passes with `posix-api.args` gone.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it (comment citing the job logs above).\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the change, including the new harness classifier tests.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `posix-api.args` names a test that passed (or skipped with a capability reason) in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run, with `posix-api.args` and its `@` reference removed.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795038831764460459,"uuid":"e88b0a07-750d-4e73-81b4-57a2dfc6ae21"}